# Events on the roads of Lake Zarovich, the hills and Lake Baratok (random tables zarovich_hills, zarovich_shore).

~ howl_call
Narrator: Up in the hills a wolf howls, long and rising. Another answers it from the north, and then a third, and then the whole ridge is singing.
* [Survival DC 13] Listen to where they're coming from. -> howl_ok | howl_fail
* Keep walking. -> END

~ howl_ok
set den_way_known
Narrator: The first howl came from the rock face at the top of the pine slope, north and a little east of the lake, and every other voice is answering it. That is where they sleep.
interject name:thistle: Hear the first one? That's the boss. Grandda says find the boss and you've found the bed.
-> END

~ howl_fail
Narrator: The howls come from everywhere and nowhere, the way they do in hills. By the time they stop, you have lost track of all of them.
-> END

~ krezk_cart
Narrator: A farm cart lies on its side in the ditch, one wheel still turning slowly in the wind. No horse. No driver. In the bed of the cart, a child's coat, and a long smear leading up the slope into the trees.
* [Survival DC 12] Follow the marks a little way. -> cart_ok | cart_fail
* Leave it. -> END

~ cart_ok
set den_way_known
Narrator: The marks go up and up, north toward the rock face above the lake, and the prints beside them change, halfway, from boots to paws.
-> END

~ cart_fail
Narrator: The trail vanishes into pine needles and rock. Whatever carried the child knew this slope better than you do.
-> END

~ silver_snare
set tower_rumor
Narrator: A dead wolf hangs by one leg from a bent sapling, the snare bitten deep: silvered wire, tied with a neat, showy Vistani knot. More snares run off west, toward the little cold lake under the mountain.
interject tag:curious: Somebody out here hunts wolves for a living, and hunts them well.
-> END

~ emil_wolves
Narrator: Three grey wolves cross the trail ahead of you at a lope. The last one stops, looks at you for a long moment, and dips its head before it goes on. Emil's wolves know your smell.
-> END

~ ridge_watcher
set den_way_known
Narrator: On a ridge above the trail, a big wolf stands outlined against the sky, watching you. When it sees you looking, it turns and lopes away north, unhurried, toward the rock face above the lake.
-> END

~ drowned_bell
Narrator: From somewhere out on the water, through the mist, a bell tolls once. Then again. There is no bell on Lake Zarovich, and no church on its shores.
interject class:cleric: Somebody rang that. I'd rather not meet them.
-> END
